    "body": "## Problem\n\nNvim segfaults when the screen gets narrower while a decoration provider calls `line('w0', win)` in `on_start`.\n\nThe treesitter highlighter does exactly that in `_on_start`. So a markdown buffer in a right split is enough to hit it. I hit it twice in one day just switching tmux panes.\n\n```\n_platform_memmove\nlinecopy\ngrid_del_lines\ncurs_columns\nupdate_topline\nvar2fpos\nf_line\n...\ndecor_provider_invoke\ndecor_providers_start\nupdate_screen\n```\n\n`decor_providers_start()` runs before `win_grid_alloc()`, so during `on_start` the window's `col_offset` is still the pre-resize one. If `line('w0')` changes the topline, `curs_columns()` scrolls the window with `win_scroll_lines()`. `checked_width` goes negative and `grid_del_lines()` copies past the end of the grid.\n\nRepro with `nvim --clean -u repro.lua`:\n\n```lua\nvim.o.columns, vim.o.lines = 200, 40\nvim.cmd('rightbelow vnew')\nlocal win = vim.api.nvim_get_current_win()\nvim.api.nvim_buf_set_lines(0, 0, -1, false, { 'title', ('x'):rep(57) })\nvim.api.nvim_win_set_cursor(win, { 2, 56 })\nvim.cmd('wincmd p | vertical resize 120 | redraw')\nvim.api.nvim_set_decoration_provider(vim.api.nvim_create_namespace('t'), {\n  on_start = function() vim.fn.line('w0', win) end,\n})\nvim.o.columns = 100\nvim.cmd('redraw')\n```\n\nCrashes on 0.12.1 and on master (544d8cd). Similar stack : #22278.\n\n## Solution\n\nReturn early from `win_scroll_lines()` when `checked_width <= 0`. The window gets a full redraw after the resize anyway, so skipping the scroll loses nothing.\n\nThis fixes the crash, not the root cause : window offsets are still stale during `on_start`. Calling `win_grid_alloc()` before `decor_providers_start()`, or not scrolling the grid from `curs_columns()` at all (the TODO there), would fix that. Happy to switch to one of those if you prefer.\n",
